# psg_tone.checks - one row per CHECK of fixtures/src/psg_tone.s (D-125, plan 05-04, grown by 05-06). Columns separated by one TAB: check index (1-based), slug, class tag, meaning.
# The PSG is write only (H8-24): these checks judge the guest's own table data with two in-guest computations each (GUEST); every judgement of the sound is the runner's, against fixtures/src/psg_tone.aexp (ER-21). A pass is not a support claim (ER-4).
id=27
checks=10
1	table-sum-low	GUEST:table-sum	The low byte of the sum of the 32 table words (a table walk) equals the low byte of the sum of the counter 0..31: 496 = $01F0, low byte $F0
2	table-sum-high	GUEST:table-sum	The high byte of the same two sums: $01
3	table-order	GUEST:table-order	Words 0..15 of the table equal the closed form 16 + 3i (i = 0..5), 29 - 3(i - 6) (i = 6..10), 18 + 3(i - 11) (i = 11..15): the OR of the differences is zero
4	table-perm	GUEST:table-perm	The 32 words are a permutation of 0..31: a bit per value in four map bytes, all set (the AND of the bytes is $FF)
5	table-sum-0	GUEST:table-sum	Channel table 0 (select 0) summed by a table walk equals the sum of the counter 0..31 (496): the low bytes XOR and the high bytes XOR, ORed, are zero
6	table-sum-1	GUEST:table-sum	Channel table 1 (select 1) summed by a table walk equals the sum of the counter 0..31 (496): the low bytes XOR and the high bytes XOR, ORed, are zero
7	table-sum-2	GUEST:table-sum	Channel table 2 (select 2) summed by a table walk equals the sum of the counter 0..31 (496): the low bytes XOR and the high bytes XOR, ORed, are zero
8	table-sum-3	GUEST:table-sum	Channel table 3 (select 3) summed by a table walk equals the sum of the counter 0..31 (496): the low bytes XOR and the high bytes XOR, ORed, are zero
9	table-sum-4	GUEST:table-sum	Channel table 4 (select 4) summed by a table walk equals the sum of the counter 0..31 (496): the low bytes XOR and the high bytes XOR, ORed, are zero
10	table-sum-5	GUEST:table-sum	Channel table 5 (select 5) summed by a table walk equals the sum of the counter 0..31 (496): the low bytes XOR and the high bytes XOR, ORed, are zero
